#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068508 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54bab77-d77f-5275-b454-ddb565eaa280" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Indefinite Integral of a Rational Function Using Partial Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "f374b567-9a69-57ae-88eb-644ebfc451d7" :question/math-academy-id "e-506" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int \\dfrac{5x}{x^2+3x-4} \\,\\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\nx^2+3x-4 = (x-1)(x+4) \\,\n$$\n\nSo, the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{5x}{x^{2} + 3x - 4} &= (5x)/((x - 1)(x + 4)) \\\\\n&= (A)/((x - 1)) + (B)/((x + 4))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5x &= A(x + 4) + B(x - 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-4$, we can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5(-4) &= A(-4 + 4) + B(-4 - 1) \\\\\n- 20 &= -5B \\\\\nB &= 4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, by plugging in $x=1$, we can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5(1) &= A(1 + 4) + B(1 - 1) \\\\\n5 &= 5A \\\\\nA &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{5x}{x^2+3x-4} = \\dfrac{1}{(x-1)} +\\dfrac{4}{(x+4)}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate, and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{5x}{x^{2} + 3x - 4}dx &= ∫(\\frac{1}{x - 1} + \\frac{4}{x + 4})dx \\\\\n&= ∫\\frac{1}{x - 1}dx + 4∫\\frac{1}{x + 4}dx \\\\\n&= \\ln\\begin{vmatrix}x - 1 & + 4\\ln & x + 4\\end{vmatrix}+ C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068510 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "771dfcc1-f6c3-59ed-8961-3fe477b011b6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Definite Integral of a Rational Function Using Partial Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "fce14198-c8ee-50a6-981d-85df79cce761" :question/math-academy-id "e-507" :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_1^4 \\dfrac{2x+3}{4x^2-1} \\,\\textrm{d}x$." :question/worked-solution "We'll work out the indefinite integral first and then proceed with the definite integral.\n\nFirst, we note that a denominator of the integrand can be factored as\n\n$$\n4x^2-1 = (2x+1)(2x-1) \\,\n$$\n\nSo the integrand can be converted into a sum of partial fractions,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{2x + 3}{4x^{2} - 1} &= (2x + 3)/((2x + 1)(2x - 1)) \\\\\n&= (A)/((2x + 1)) + (B)/((2x - 1))\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2x + 3 &= A(2x - 1) + B(2x + 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPlugging in\n\n$$\nx=\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nwe can eliminate $A$ and solve for $B$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(\\frac{1}{2}) + 3 &= A(2(\\frac{1}{2}) - 1) + B(2(\\frac{1}{2}) + 1) \\\\\n4 &= 2B \\\\\nB &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in\n\n$$\nx=-\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nwe can eliminate $B$ and solve for $A$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(-\\frac{1}{2}) + 3 &= A(2(-\\frac{1}{2}) - 1) + B(2(-\\frac{1}{2}) + 1) \\\\\n2 &= -2A \\\\\nA &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x+3}{4x^2-1} = -\\dfrac{1}{(2x+1)} +\\dfrac{2}{(2x-1)}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{2x + 3}{4x^{2} - 1}dx &= ∫(- (1)/((2x + 1)) + (2)/((2x - 1)))dx \\\\\n&= - ∫\\frac{1}{2x + 1}dx + 2∫\\frac{1}{2x - 1}dx \\\\\n&=-\\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}2x + 1 & + 2(\\frac{1}{2}\\ln \\mid 2x - 1 \\mid) + C \\\\ =-\\frac{1}{2}\\ln & 2x + 1\\end{vmatrix}+ \\ln \\mid 2x - 1 \\mid + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify the result using the laws of logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫\\frac{2x + 3}{4x^{2} - 1}dx &= -\\frac{1}{2}\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}2x + 1 & + \\ln & 2x - 1 & + C \\\\ = \\ln & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2x + 1}} & + \\ln & 2x - 1\\end{vmatrix}+ C \\\\\n&= \\ln \\mid \\frac{2x - 1}{\\sqrt{2x + 1}} \\mid + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the definite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_{1}^{4}\\frac{2x + 3}{4x^{2} - 1}dx &= \\ln \\mid \\frac{2x - 1}{\\sqrt{2x + 1}} \\mid _{1}^{4} \\\\\n&= \\ln (\\frac{7}{3}) - \\ln (\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\\n&= \\ln (\\frac{7}{3}) + \\ln (\\sqrt{3}) \\\\\n&= \\ln (\\frac{7\\sqrt{3}}{3})\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d54bab77-d77f-5275-b454-ddb565eaa280" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating an Indefinite Integral of a Rational Function Using Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b2ab0f3a-4e41-524f-bd9e-03c46311722b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067332} {:answer/id #uuid "c255a472-9b1a-56de-baec-93fc501ee751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067333} {:answer/id #uuid "c9f7b7a9-f5dc-5e8b-81ea-22c5213943d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067334} {:answer/id #uuid "17efe871-acac-5c1b-affc-45c1fa349a36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067335} {:answer/id #uuid "4b41ab18-e879-5684-9158-ed41d186f5c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c255a472-9b1a-56de-baec-93fc501ee751" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067333} :answer-field/id #uuid "c334a28a-25dc-5066-8861-a6d8339b2304" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067331}] :question/id #uuid "1f6ebcba-4e39-5954-8ee8-c37c592d0f6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-49604" :question/problem "Given that\n\n$∫(13)/((3x + 2)(2x - 3))dx = a\\ln\\begin{vmatrix}2x - 3 & + b\\ln & 3x + 2\\end{vmatrix}+ C$,\nfind the value of $a + b$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069303 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "771dfcc1-f6c3-59ed-8961-3fe477b011b6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Definite Integral of a Rational Function Using Partial Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d056e470-bbb9-5efb-b3f7-6cdfec45ac75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (\\frac{7}{32})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067350} {:answer/id #uuid "e55741ee-a7df-58bb-b3d1-29e8c87a8db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (17)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067351} {:answer/id #uuid "0ace05db-2ed0-5e1d-af7d-be3349a9a280" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (168)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067352} {:answer/id #uuid "175944fd-56bb-51ab-86fe-5afb691675a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (\\frac{7}{36})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067353} {:answer/id #uuid "6a00476a-749c-5bf2-8c69-b7b60c40a397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (\\frac{7}{24})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a00476a-749c-5bf2-8c69-b7b60c40a397" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\ln (\\frac{7}{24})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067354} :answer-field/id #uuid "6cba9533-abbc-5460-b1bf-3b10532ae935" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186067349}] :question/id #uuid "1b7a0d53-d8cd-5e6c-b6e9-1877172e8d87" :question/math-academy-id "q-49761" :question/problem "Evaluate\n\n$∫_{2}^{3}\\frac{3x + 4}{x^{2} - 16}dx$."}]}
